      ":question/worked-solution": "For two distinct nonvertical lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\nTo find the slope of $-10x-2y=-6$, convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-10x-2y &= -6 \\\\\n-2y &= 10x-6 \\\\\ny &= -5x+3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope is the coefficient of $x$, so the required slope is $-5$.\n\nOnly $y=-5x-4$ has slope $-5$.\n\nThe line $y=-5x-4$ has slope $-5$ and $y$-intercept $-4$, different from $3$. Therefore, it is a distinct parallel line.\n\n$$\ny=-5x-4\n$$",
